Run test-filesys-cdvdfs-cache or test-filesys-cdvdfs-cache-quick through the
filesystem test component, or invoke python3 host_test.py here.

The host harness compiles the production cache/reclamation/read functions
from CDVDFS cdrom.c. Its adapter supplies deterministic drive data and
bounded optional allocations. ASan/UBSan check the real buffer accesses.
No game image or hardware is required. The host pointer width is printed.
This is a cache-core test, not a boot test of a complete 64-bit AROS system.

The UFO-pattern case alternates between two distant file positions after
all optional caches have been reclaimed. Correct data must be returned and
only two physical reads are needed when cache memory becomes available.
Other cases cover failed/partial recovery, preserving DMA requirements,
no-expunge allocations, metadata traffic, active I/O, concurrent reclamation
during an allocator wait, and repeated memory pressure. Pass an original cdrom.c using --source and --expect-failure to
check that the original implementation fails the observable cache cases.
